  "body": "**Why:** the post-merge gate is red on main (#3111). Bisected: `motion: vertical_arc_entry` passes on `96b22c84d^1` and fails from `96b22c84d` (the merge of #3053) onward.\n\n**What #3053 did wrong:** its `lead_fit` change applies to every closed contour, not only rings with tabs. On the test's plain rectangle (no tabs):\n- the seam moved from the corner (x=4) to mid-edge (x=20);\n- the vertical G18 entry arc reversed (S1 to S-1);\n- an overlap move 20 to 23 was added.\n\nOn an oblique first cut, the chord-fan entry is gone. This changes posted G-code outside the issue's case. #3053's quick gate ran only `contour_tab_lead`, not `vertical_arc_entry`.\n\n**This PR:** `git revert -m 1 96b22c84d`. It removes the `lead_fit` change, its test and its decision file, and nothing else.\n\n**Tested (macOS arm64, on this head):**\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-motion --test vertical_arc_entry`: 3/3 pass.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-post --test vertical_arc_entry`: 3/3 pass.\n\n**Not exercised:** the full batch tier. The post-merge gate runs it after merge.\n\n**Follow-up:** #3019 is reopened, to be redone so that the seam and lead change applies only where a tab needs it, with `vertical_arc_entry` in its gate.\n\nChangelog: none (reverts an unreleased change)\n\nFixes #3111\nRefs #3019\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
